# gvisor.env — the ONE place the gVisor release is pinned (setec#89).
#
# Three consumers read this file and carry no version of their own:
#   Dockerfile.installer                          build args from .github/workflows/images.yml
#   development/k3s/scripts/*                     source it when preparing a node by hand
#   the e2e suite's node prep                     sources it
# scripts/check-runtime-pins.sh fails CI when any of them re-adds a literal.
#
# The installer lays runsc and its containerd shim onto every node, because
# nothing else does: kata-deploy does not ship gVisor, and the sanctioned kind
# profile runs gvisor as its ONE backend. Before this pin existed, a plain
# `helm install` produced a node advertising runtime.gvisor=false.
#
# To bump: change all three lines. The two SHA256 values are of the release
# binaries themselves (gVisor publishes no tarball and no combined checksum
# file, so each binary is pinned separately).
#
# Upstream publishes releases by date:
#   https://storage.googleapis.com/gvisor/releases/release/<GVISOR_VERSION>/x86_64/runsc
#   https://storage.googleapis.com/gvisor/releases/release/<GVISOR_VERSION>/x86_64/containerd-shim-runsc-v1
# zeroroot-ai/.github version-links.yaml watches upstream releases.
GVISOR_VERSION=20260915
GVISOR_RUNSC_SHA256=REPLACE_ME_RUNSC_SHA256
GVISOR_SHIM_SHA256=REPLACE_ME_SHIM_SHA256
